<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Four cells by two, which is the shape the picture actually is.

    The face is the dashboard's card — wordmark, dial, Scout beside it, four
    figures underneath — drawn at 300 by 200, so three wide by two tall. It does
    not survive being dragged into a square: fitCenter keeps the picture
    undistorted, so a square cell shows the same card with a band of nothing
    above and below it.

    ── That is not a warning any more, it is a bug report ─────────────────────

    This said four by THREE, and the paragraph above described exactly what that
    produced. The arithmetic is the whole of it: a home screen cell is taller
    than it is wide — roughly 74dp by 100 on a Pixel — so four by three is about
    296 by 300, which is a square. The picture is half as wide again as it is
    tall. Every ring widget anybody placed came out letterboxed, and the comment
    explaining why was sitting directly above the number causing it.

    Four by two is about 296 by 200. The picture is 300 by 200.

    minHeight follows, because it is the same statement for launchers too old to
    read targetCell: Android's own rule is 70n − 30, so two rows is 110dp.

    Height can still be dragged taller by anyone who wants it that way — the
    bands come back, but then they are somebody's choice rather than the default
    nobody asked for.

    No previewLayout: the layout is an empty ImageView until the app has run
    once, so a live preview would show the picker a blank rounded rectangle.
    previewImage points at the app icon, which at least says whose widget it is.
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:minWidth="250dp"
    android:minHeight="110dp"
    android:minResizeWidth="180dp"
    android:minResizeHeight="110dp"
    android:maxResizeWidth="400dp"
    android:maxResizeHeight="260dp"
    android:targetCellWidth="4"
    android:targetCellHeight="2"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/widget_ring"
    android:previewImage="@mipmap/ic_launcher"
    android:description="@string/widget_ring_description"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="0" />
